  "scope": "General relative-extremal definition in Chapter 1; complete affine/projective subsection at the recorded mixed fresh/reused first-read scope and fresh seven-input final second read. Complete 259-line capacity root and Chapter 33 seam79--92 freshly reread after 34 actual final images. No new whole recursive Chapter 1/12/33 certification.",
  "mathematical_boundary": "Relative/global zero-value comparison is proved by direct logarithmic pasting and the accepted pole barrier. Local pluriregularity gives local weighted regularity for bounded USC weights with global raw contact. A continuous global extending weight in L_tau, locally bounded below in Hessian by c omega0, gives a quantitative contact defect and exact regularity persistence for delta>=tau. The C2 Hessian degeneracy consequence is pointwise. No general product formula, thinness/plurifine classification, novelty or original-problem closure is claimed.",
